{%- comment -%}
  Product card — a line of text the merchant writes or binds.

  **One block for every fixed thing a card says.** It replaced two: a
  metafield-only caption line and a tax note that carried its own copy. Both
  were the same element with different words, and one of them had a jeweller's
  vocabulary built in.

  Three uses, all of them the same block:

    - a fact about the piece — connect the text to a product metafield with the
      dynamic-source button and it prints whatever that shop keeps there;
    - a separator — a `·` between two other blocks inside a `group`, which is
      how "White Gold · 1.5 ct" is composed now rather than assembled in Liquid;
    - an aside beside the price, which is what the tax note became.

  **The text is a dynamic source, not a metafield picker.** Shopify has no
  metafield setting type for a block schema; what it has is the dynamic-source
  connector on a `text` setting, and inside this static card it binds against
  `closest.product` — the same context every other block here reads.

  **Every control is an override and none of them is required.** Left alone the
  block is the card's caption: the theme's micro size, its meta tracking,
  uppercase, and ink at 72%. Each setting replaces exactly one of those and
  emits nothing when it is set to inherit, so the block's own stylesheet rule
  stays the single description of what a caption looks like.

  The sizes are the theme's **product-text tokens**, not lengths — the same
  four `--product-*` properties the title, the caption and the price are drawn
  from. A merchant picks "as large as the price", not a number, and a shop that
  retunes its type scale moves this with everything else. That is the rule this
  theme is built to: nothing hardcodes a size.

  **The row is held whether or not there is a word in it.** `.card__meta`'s
  `min-height: 1.5em` is what keeps a row of cards level when one piece has a
  fact and its neighbour does not, and it is why a block bound to a metafield
  one product is missing still shows as an empty line rather than collapsing.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign value = block.settings.text

  comment
    Each override emits one declaration, or nothing at all. Nothing is the
    important half: an unset control has to leave the stylesheet's own value
    standing rather than restate it, or the class stops being the one place a
    caption is described.
  endcomment
  assign style = ''

  case block.settings.font
    when 'body'
      assign style = style | append: 'font-family: var(--font-body);'
    when 'heading'
      assign style = style | append: 'font-family: var(--font-heading);'
  endcase

  case block.settings.size
    when 'xs'
      assign style = style | append: 'font-size: calc(var(--micro-size) * 0.85);'
    when 'note'
      comment
        The theme's own price-note relationship — `.price-tax` is `0.75em` of
        the price it follows, and this is that same figure stated where the
        note is no longer inside the price element to inherit it from.
      endcomment
      assign style = style | append: 'font-size: calc(var(--product-price-size) * 0.75);'
    when 'sm'
      assign style = style | append: 'font-size: var(--micro-size);'
    when 'md'
      assign style = style | append: 'font-size: var(--product-price-size);'
    when 'lg'
      assign style = style | append: 'font-size: var(--product-title-size);'
    when 'xl'
      assign style = style | append: 'font-size: calc(var(--product-title-size) * 1.35);'
  endcase

  case block.settings.text_transform
    when 'uppercase'
      assign style = style | append: 'text-transform: uppercase;'
    when 'lowercase'
      assign style = style | append: 'text-transform: lowercase;'
    when 'capitalize'
      assign style = style | append: 'text-transform: capitalize;'
    when 'none'
      assign style = style | append: 'text-transform: none;'
  endcase

  comment
    "Muted" is a relative expression rather than a colour, so it follows
    whatever scheme the card is in — the same treatment the price note has
    always had. A picked colour is absolute by definition and is the merchant's
    to get right on every scheme they use.
  endcomment
  case block.settings.color_source
    when 'muted'
      assign style = style | append: 'color: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 62%, transparent);'
    when 'custom'
      if block.settings.custom_color != blank
        assign style = style | append: 'color: ' | append: block.settings.custom_color | append: ';'
      endif
  endcase
-%}

<span class="card__meta card__text" style="{{ style }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
  {{- value -}}
</span>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:blocks.product_card_text.name",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "text",
      "label": "t:blocks.product_card_text.text.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.product_card_text.text.info"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:blocks.product_card_text.type_header"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "font",
      "label": "t:blocks.product_card_text.font.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "inherit", "label": "t:blocks.all.inherit.label" },
        { "value": "body", "label": "t:blocks.product_card_text.font.body" },
        { "value": "heading", "label": "t:blocks.product_card_text.font.heading" }
      ],
      "default": "inherit"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "size",
      "label": "t:blocks.product_card_text.size.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.product_card_text.size.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "inherit", "label": "t:blocks.all.inherit.label" },
        { "value": "xs", "label": "t:blocks.product_card_text.size.xs" },
        { "value": "note", "label": "t:blocks.product_card_text.size.note" },
        { "value": "sm", "label": "t:blocks.product_card_text.size.sm" },
        { "value": "md", "label": "t:blocks.product_card_text.size.md" },
        { "value": "lg", "label": "t:blocks.product_card_text.size.lg" },
        { "value": "xl", "label": "t:blocks.product_card_text.size.xl" }
      ],
      "default": "inherit"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "text_transform",
      "label": "t:blocks.product_card_text.text_transform.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "inherit", "label": "t:blocks.all.inherit.label" },
        { "value": "uppercase", "label": "t:blocks.product_card_text.text_transform.uppercase" },
        { "value": "lowercase", "label": "t:blocks.product_card_text.text_transform.lowercase" },
        { "value": "capitalize", "label": "t:blocks.product_card_text.text_transform.capitalize" },
        { "value": "none", "label": "t:blocks.product_card_text.text_transform.none" }
      ],
      "default": "inherit"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "color_source",
      "label": "t:blocks.product_card_text.color_source.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.product_card_text.color_source.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "inherit", "label": "t:blocks.all.inherit.label" },
        { "value": "muted", "label": "t:blocks.product_card_text.color_source.muted" },
        { "value": "custom", "label": "t:blocks.product_card_text.color_source.custom" }
      ],
      "default": "inherit"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "custom_color",
      "label": "t:blocks.product_card_text.custom_color.label",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.color_source == 'custom' }}"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "t:blocks.product_card_text.name",
      "settings": {
        "text": "Text"
      }
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
